    {"id":"local_062","title":"Annunciation","artist":"Leonardo da Vinci","year":1472,"period":"Early Renaissance","style":"Oil and tempera on panel","medium":"Oil and tempera on wood panel","dimensions":"98 cm x 217 cm","origin":"Uffizi Gallery, Florence","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Leonardo's early masterpiece depicting the Angel Gabriel announcing to the Virgin Mary that she will conceive the Son of God.","historicalContext":"Painted when Leonardo was a young artist in Verrocchio's workshop, showing his emerging mastery of atmospheric perspective.","meaning":"The Annunciation represents the pivotal moment when divine purpose is revealed to humanity through Mary's acceptance.","keySymbols":["lily","angel wings","lectern","walled garden"],"creditLine":"Uffizi Gallery, Florence","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_063","title":"Salvator Mundi","artist":"Leonardo da Vinci","year":1500,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on walnut panel","medium":"Oil on walnut panel","dimensions":"65.6 cm x 45.4 cm","origin":"Private Collection","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Salvator Mundi portrays Christ as Saviour of the World, holding a crystal orb in his left hand while raising his right hand in blessing.","historicalContext":"Rediscovered in 2005 and authenticated as a Leonardo original. Sold for a record $450 million in 2017.","meaning":"Christ is shown as sovereign ruler of the cosmos. The crystal orb symbolizes the celestial sphere under divine dominion.","keySymbols":["crystal orb","blessing hand","blue robe","sfumato"],"creditLine":"Department of Culture and Tourism, Abu Dhabi","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_064","title":"Madonna of Bruges","artist":"Michelangelo","year":1504,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Marble sculpture","medium":"Marble","dimensions":"128 cm (height)","origin":"Church of Our Lady, Bruges","type":"Sculpture","subject":"Religious","description":"A marble sculpture of the Virgin Mary with the infant Jesus. Mary does not clasp the child but lets him stand between her knees.","historicalContext":"One of the few Michelangelo sculptures to leave Italy during his lifetime, purchased by Bruges merchants.","meaning":"Mary's calm expression suggests her foreknowledge of Christ's suffering. The child stepping away symbolizes his future sacrifice.","keySymbols":["standing child","serene Madonna","draped clothing","marble"],"creditLine":"Church of Our Lady, Bruges, Belgium","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_065","title":"Madonna del Granduca","artist":"Raphael","year":1505,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on panel","medium":"Oil on panel","dimensions":"84 cm x 55 cm","origin":"Palazzo Pitti, Florence","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"A tender depiction of the Virgin Mary holding the infant Christ against a dark background, showcasing Raphael's mastery of gentle form.","historicalContext":"Named after Grand Duke Ferdinand III of Tuscany, who loved the painting so much he carried it when traveling.","meaning":"The painting embodies maternal love and divine grace through the intimate bond between mother and child.","keySymbols":["dark background","tender embrace","soft light","red and blue robes"],"creditLine":"Palazzo Pitti, Florence","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_066","title":"Adoration of the Magi","artist":"Sandro Botticelli","year":1475,"period":"Early Renaissance","style":"Tempera on panel","medium":"Tempera on wood panel","dimensions":"111 cm x 134 cm","origin":"Uffizi Gallery, Florence","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"The three wise men presenting gifts to the infant Jesus, with portraits of the Medici family among the crowd.","historicalContext":"Commissioned by Gaspare di Zanobi del Lama for Santa Maria Novella. Served as political propaganda for the Medici dynasty.","meaning":"By depicting the Medici as the Magi, Botticelli elevated his patrons to biblical status.","keySymbols":["Medici portraits","ruins","self-portrait","gifts"],"creditLine":"Uffizi Gallery, Florence","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_067","title":"Mystic Nativity","artist":"Sandro Botticelli","year":1500,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"108.6 cm x 74.9 cm","origin":"National Gallery, London","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Botticelli's only signed painting shows the Nativity with angels dancing above and demons fleeing below.","historicalContext":"Painted during Savonarola's influence in Florence. The Greek inscription references the Book of Revelation.","meaning":"Expresses Botticelli's belief in an imminent apocalypse and spiritual renewal.","keySymbols":["dancing angels","fleeing demons","Greek inscription","olive branches"],"creditLine":"National Gallery, London","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_068","title":"Venus and Mars","artist":"Sandro Botticelli","year":1485,"period":"Early Renaissance","style":"Tempera and oil on panel","medium":"Tempera and oil on poplar panel","dimensions":"69 cm x 173.4 cm","origin":"National Gallery, London","type":"Painting","subject":"Mythology","description":"Venus watches over sleeping Mars while playful satyrs steal his weapons, symbolizing love's triumph over war.","historicalContext":"Likely painted for a Florentine wedding, possibly for the Vespucci family. The elongated format suggests a spalliera.","meaning":"An allegory of love conquering war. Venus remains alert while Mars lies defeated by passion.","keySymbols":["sleeping Mars","alert Venus","satyrs with lance","wasps"],"creditLine":"National Gallery, London","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_069","title":"Bacchus and Ariadne","artist":"Titian","year":1523,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"176.5 cm x 191 cm","origin":"National Gallery, London","type":"Painting","subject":"Mythology","description":"Bacchus leaps from his chariot toward Ariadne, abandoned by Theseus on Naxos. The sky shows her future constellation.","historicalContext":"Painted for Alfonso I d'Este's camerino in Ferrara, part of a cycle of mythological paintings.","meaning":"The painting captures the moment when mortal sorrow becomes divine joy through love with a god.","keySymbols":["leaping Bacchus","constellation Corona","cheetahs","thyrsus"],"creditLine":"National Gallery, London","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_070","title":"Pesaro Madonna","artist":"Titian","year":1526,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"478 cm x 266.5 cm","origin":"Santa Maria Gloriosa dei Frari, Venice","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"An innovative altarpiece with the Madonna placed off-center in a revolutionary asymmetric composition with the Pesaro family.","historicalContext":"Commissioned by Bishop Jacopo Pesaro. Titian broke tradition by placing the Madonna to the right instead of center.","meaning":"The asymmetric composition creates dynamic movement, drawing the eye diagonally toward the Madonna.","keySymbols":["off-center Madonna","massive columns","Turkish flag","Pesaro family"],"creditLine":"Basilica dei Frari, Venice","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_071","title":"Danae","artist":"Titian","year":1553,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"129.8 cm x 181.2 cm","origin":"Museo del Prado, Madrid","type":"Painting","subject":"Mythology","description":"Danae reclines as Zeus visits her in a shower of golden coins. An old servant tries to catch the gold.","historicalContext":"Created for Philip II of Spain, representing the pinnacle of Titian's late coloristic style.","meaning":"The myth explores themes of desire, fate, and divine intervention. The golden rain symbolizes both divine love and corrupting wealth.","keySymbols":["golden rain","reclining nude","old servant","dark clouds"],"creditLine":"Museo del Prado, Madrid","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_072","title":"Knight, Death and the Devil","artist":"Albrecht Durer","year":1513,"period":"Northern Renaissance","style":"Engraving","medium":"Engraving on laid paper","dimensions":"24.6 cm x 19.1 cm","origin":"Various collections","type":"Print","subject":"Allegory","description":"A Christian knight rides steadfastly through a dark valley, ignoring Death with an hourglass and the Devil lurking behind.","historicalContext":"One of Durer's three master engravings along with Melencolia I and St. Jerome in His Study.","meaning":"The knight represents the Christian soul's journey through life, steadfast in faith despite temptation and death.","keySymbols":["hourglass","dog","castle on hill","skull"],"creditLine":"Various museums","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_073","title":"Saint Mark","artist":"Donatello","year":1413,"period":"Early Renaissance","style":"Marble sculpture","medium":"Marble","dimensions":"236 cm (height)","origin":"Orsanmichele, Florence","type":"Sculpture","subject":"Religious","description":"A monumental marble statue of Saint Mark in contrapposto pose. Michelangelo said he would believe the Gospel preached by such a figure.","historicalContext":"Commissioned by the Linen Drapers' Guild for an exterior niche of Orsanmichele in Florence.","meaning":"Marks a turning point in Renaissance sculpture, replacing Gothic rigidity with naturalistic weight distribution.","keySymbols":["Gospel book","contrapposto","draped toga","intense gaze"],"creditLine":"Museo di Orsanmichele, Florence","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_074","title":"Judith and Holofernes","artist":"Donatello","year":1460,"period":"Early Renaissance","style":"Bronze sculpture","medium":"Bronze","dimensions":"236 cm (height)","origin":"Palazzo Vecchio, Florence","type":"Sculpture","subject":"Religious","description":"Judith about to deliver the killing blow to the Assyrian general Holofernes. A symbol of republican liberty.","historicalContext":"Originally in the Palazzo Medici garden, moved to Piazza della Signoria after the Medici expulsion in 1495.","meaning":"Judith represents virtue triumphing over tyranny - humility defeating pride.","keySymbols":["raised sword","Holofernes head","cushion","triangular composition"],"creditLine":"Palazzo Vecchio, Florence","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_075","title":"Portrait of Henry VIII","artist":"Hans Holbein the Younger","year":1537,"period":"Northern Renaissance","style":"Oil on panel","medium":"Oil and tempera on oak panel","dimensions":"28 cm x 20 cm","origin":"Thyssen-Bornemisza Museum, Madrid","type":"Painting","subject":"Portrait","description":"A powerful frontal portrait of King Henry VIII in sumptuous royal attire, projecting absolute authority.","historicalContext":"Based on the famous Whitehall mural destroyed in 1698. This is the closest surviving version.","meaning":"The frontal pose, broad shoulders, and rich costume project absolute royal power as political propaganda.","keySymbols":["jeweled costume","frontal pose","broad shoulders","royal insignia"],"creditLine":"Thyssen-Bornemisza Museum, Madrid","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_076","title":"The Feast in the House of Levi","artist":"Paolo Veronese","year":1573,"period":"Mannerism","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"555 cm x 1280 cm","origin":"Gallerie dell'Accademia, Venice","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Originally titled The Last Supper, this monumental banquet scene includes jesters, dwarfs, and soldiers in Palladian architecture.","historicalContext":"The Inquisition charged Veronese with irreverence. He simply renamed it rather than repaint.","meaning":"Celebrates Venetian splendor. The defiant renaming shows artistic independence from religious authority.","keySymbols":["Palladian architecture","diverse crowd","dogs and jesters","grand staircase"],"creditLine":"Gallerie dell'Accademia, Venice","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_077","title":"The Calling of Saint Matthew","artist":"Caravaggio","year":1600,"period":"Mannerism","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"322 cm x 340 cm","origin":"San Luigi dei Francesi, Rome","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Christ and Saint Peter enter a dimly lit room where Matthew sits with companions. A dramatic shaft of light follows Christ's gesture.","historicalContext":"Caravaggio's first major public commission. It shocked Rome with contemporary clothing and dramatic chiaroscuro.","meaning":"The beam of light represents divine grace. Christ's gesture echoes Michelangelo's Creation of Adam.","keySymbols":["shaft of light","pointing hand","coins on table","contemporary dress"],"creditLine":"San Luigi dei Francesi, Rome","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_078","title":"Judith Beheading Holofernes","artist":"Caravaggio","year":1599,"period":"Mannerism","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"145 cm x 195 cm","origin":"Galleria Nazionale d'Arte Antica, Rome","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Judith beheads Holofernes in a scene of intense violence illuminated by harsh, dramatic light.","historicalContext":"Painted for Roman banker Ottavio Costa. The unflinching realism revolutionized how biblical violence was depicted.","meaning":"Judith embodies righteous courage against tyranny. Caravaggio's realism forces viewers to confront heroic action's brutal reality.","keySymbols":["sword","spurting blood","old maidservant","dark background"],"creditLine":"Galleria Nazionale d'Arte Antica, Rome","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_079","title":"The Tempest","artist":"Giorgione","year":1508,"period":"High Renaissance","style":"Oil on canvas","medium":"Oil on canvas","dimensions":"82 cm x 73 cm","origin":"Gallerie dell'Accademia, Venice","type":"Painting","subject":"Allegory","description":"A mysterious landscape with a soldier and a nursing woman separated by a stream, while lightning flashes over a city.","historicalContext":"One of the most debated paintings in art history. X-rays reveal Giorgione originally painted a different figure.","meaning":"The meaning remains enigmatic - interpretations range from Adam and Eve to allegories of nature.","keySymbols":["lightning","broken columns","nursing woman","bridge"],"creditLine":"Gallerie dell'Accademia, Venice","isPublicDomain":True},
