    {"id":"local_085","title":"St. Francis in Ecstasy","artist":"Giovanni Bellini","year":1480,"period":"Early Renaissance","style":"Oil on panel","medium":"Oil and tempera on poplar panel","dimensions":"124.4 cm x 141.9 cm","origin":"The Frick Collection, New York","type":"Painting","subject":"Religious","description":"Saint Francis stands outside his rocky hermitage with arms outstretched, bathed in warm light amidst detailed landscape.","historicalContext":"One of Bellini's masterpieces. May depict Francis receiving the stigmata or communing with God through nature.","meaning":"The luminous landscape embodies Francis's spiritual vision. All creation radiates divine presence.","keySymbols":["outstretched arms","lectern with skull","donkey","luminous landscape"],"creditLine":"The Frick Collection, New York","isPublicDomain":True},
    {"id":"local_086","title":"Portrait of a Man in a Red Turban","artist":"Jan van Eyck","year":1433,"period":"Northern Renaissance","style":"Oil on panel","medium":"Oil on oak panel","dimensions":"25.5 cm x 19 cm","origin":"National Gallery, London","type":"Painting","subject":"Portrait","description":"An intense three-quarter view portrait of a man in a red chaperon turban, believed to be van Eyck's self-portrait.","historicalContext":"The inscribed frame reads 'Als Ich Kan' (As I Can) - van Eyck's personal motto.","meaning":"The direct gaze creates unprecedented psychological intimacy, asserting artistic individuality.","keySymbols":["red turban","direct gaze","inscribed frame","three-quarter pose"],"creditLine":"National Gallery, London","isPublicDomain":True},
